Do not probe GCC-only macros to decide the float word order.

`__FLOAT_WORD_ORDER__` and `__ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__` are GCC/Clang predefined
macros. With MSVC neither exists, and cairo's probe cannot tell "both
undefined" from "both big endian", so configure defined FLOAT_WORDS_BIGENDIAN
on little-endian x86/x64 targets (confirmed in
build/vcpkg-buildtrees/cairo/x64-windows-rel/config.h). That makes
_cairo_fixed_from_double() return the *high* word of its magic-number union --
a constant 0x42B80000 -- instead of the low word, so every coordinate cairo
receives collapses to a single point: paths become degenerate, clips become
empty, and nothing is ever painted, with no cairo error status anywhere.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -187,16 +187,13 @@
   conf.set('WORDS_BIGENDIAN', 1)
 endif
 
-float_order = cc.get_define('__FLOAT_WORD_ORDER__')
-if float_order != ''
-  if float_order == cc.get_define('__ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__')
-    conf.set('FLOAT_WORDS_BIGENDIAN', 1)
-  endif
-else
-  # Assume same as platform endian
-  if host_machine.endian() == 'big'
-    conf.set('FLOAT_WORDS_BIGENDIAN', 1)
-  endif
+# The float word order matches the integer word order on every target cairo
+# supports. Do not probe __FLOAT_WORD_ORDER__/__ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__: those are
+# GCC/Clang-only, and with MSVC the probe cannot tell "both undefined" from
+# "both big endian", which defined FLOAT_WORDS_BIGENDIAN on little-endian
+# x86/x64 builds.
+if host_machine.endian() == 'big'
+  conf.set('FLOAT_WORDS_BIGENDIAN', 1)
 endif
 
 lzo_dep = dependency('lzo2', required: get_option('lzo'))
